    "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-worksp-6": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-worksp-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The workspace's app seam is pure data plus slots, as the Viewer Model's prop contract defines it. Row → app-object matching, deletion rules, and fetching stay in the host. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "statusClass",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " defaults to "
        },
        {
          "insert": "defaultTraceStatusClass",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "workspace/KernelTraceWorkspace.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), the union of both shipped hosts' status vocabularies.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The rejected alternative, hosts forking the workspace or the workspace calling back into host data layers, is how each app grows its own drifting copy. Data-and-slots keeps one workspace serving every host.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/workspace/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and any future workspace surface, which must take data and expose slots rather than reach into a host."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-hosts-exte-7": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-hosts-exte-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Hosts extend the trace viewer only through the named seams the Viewer Model defines. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/KernelTraceViewer.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " declares them as props; the shell adds no host-specific prop.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": A host that needs more control composes "
        },
        {
          "insert": "viewer-ui",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " directly. Widening the shell per host request, the rejected alternative, would make it every host's union.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/KernelTraceViewer.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " props, and every seam added later, which must be data or a named slot."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-drill-8": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-drill-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The drill-in split defaults to 40/60 tree/detail. Dragging the divider clamps the tree column to 25–65% of the width ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "KernelTraceViewer.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ").\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Reading happens on the detail side, so it gets the majority by default; an even split, the rejected default, starves the surface the panel exists to serve.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/KernelTraceViewer.tsx",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-style-system-seams-9": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-style-system-seams-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Style system seams"
        }
      ],
