    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-style-10": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-style-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The style system lives in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "viewer-shell/src/style/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": one rail shared by every host, extracted from the example app.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The rejected status quo was a rail fork per app; every host composing the viewer packages now runs the same one.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/style/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (settings, rail panel, overlay, rail state, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "style-system.css",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), and any new user-facing style control, which joins the rail rather than a host."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-per-ap-11": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-the-per-ap-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": The per-app seam is "
        },
        {
          "insert": "StyleSystemConfig",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (below). Every load/save/merge/emission entry point takes a config.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Two hosts on different Tailwind majors cannot share one token format, and two apps must never bleed into each other's storage; a single global config, the rejected alternative, would do both.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/style/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and every future entry point that reads or writes style state, which must take the config rather than assume one."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-style-system-config-shape": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-style-system-config-shape",
      "type": "state-shape",
      "props": {
        "description": "One per host app. The example app's instance is RESEARCH_STYLE_CONFIG in examples/simple-research-kernel/src/lib/style-settings.ts.",
        "example": "{\"settingsStorageKey\":\"simpleResearchStyleSettings.v1\",\"railCollapsedStorageKey\":\"simpleResearchStyleRailCollapsed\",\"railWidthStorageKey\":\"simpleResearchStyleRailWidth\",\"defaultTheme\":\"light\",\"neutralTokenFormat\":\"triplet\"}",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "settingsStorageKey",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "localStorage key for the settings blob. Keep it stable across releases."
          },
          {
            "name": "railCollapsedStorageKey",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "localStorage key for the rail's collapsed state."
          },
          {
            "name": "railWidthStorageKey",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "localStorage key for the rail width."
          },
          {
            "name": "defaultTheme",
            "type": "\"light\" | \"dark\"",
            "description": "Theme for a fresh install, or for a settings blob saved before themes existed."
          },
          {
            "name": "neutralTokenFormat",
            "type": "\"triplet\" | \"hex\"",
            "description": "Format of the shared-name neutrals (--background, --foreground, …). triplet serves Tailwind v3 rgb(var(--x)/<alpha>); hex serves Tailwind v4 @theme inline. Viewer-only tokens (status-*, trace-*, agentprism-*) are always emitted as RGB triplets."
          },
          {
            "name": "sections",
            "type": "(\"colors\" | \"effects\" | \"trace\" | \"layout\")[]",
            "required": false,
            "description": "Rail tabs to show; omitted shows all. The first entry is the fallback tab. Leaving out \"layout\" also stops the --research-* layout variables."
          }
        ],
        "name": "StyleSystemConfig",
        "source": {
          "path": "packages/viewer-shell/src/style/style-settings.ts",
          "symbol": "StyleSystemConfig"
        }
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-everything-12": {
      "id": "b-40-workspace-shell-decision-everything-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": Everything the style system produces is emitted as CSS variables that viewer classes consume with baked fallbacks. Layout geometry is an example-app knob: the style system emits "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--research-layout-padding",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--research-workspace-height",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--research-workspace-min-height",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "--research-header-height",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " only when the config shows the LAYOUT rail section, and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "examples/simple-research-kernel/src/styles.css",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " declares their defaults. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "KernelTraceWorkspace",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " reads the workspace height, min-height, and header-height variables with fallbacks.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Why",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": A host that mounts nothing still gets the default look. Requiring host wiring, the rejected alternative, makes the default experience a setup task.\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "Applies to",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/style/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "src/workspace/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and any new themable value."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
